  journal  = "Cold Spring Harbor Laboratory",
  pages    = "2021.01.28.428663",
  abstract = "The mutational profile of a cancer reflects the activity of the
              mutagenic processes which have been operative throughout the
              lineage of the cancer cell. These processes leave characteristic
              profiles of somatic mutations called mutational signatures.
              Mutational signatures, including single-based substitution (SBS)
              signatures, may reflect the effects of exogenous or endogenous
