              outcome predictions made using clinical factors. METHODS: We
              analyzed sequencing data from the over 10,000 cancer patients
              available through The Cancer Genome Atlas to identify germline
              variants associated with patient outcome using multivariate Cox
              regression models. RESULTS: We identified 79 prognostic germline
              variants in individual cancers and 112 prognostic germline
              variants in groups of cancers. The germline variants identified in
              individual cancers provide additional predictive power about
              patient outcomes beyond clinical information currently in use and
              may therefore augment clinical decisions based on expected tumor
              aggressiveness. Molecularly, at least 12 of the germline variants
