  journal  = "Genome Med.",
  volume   =  14,
  number   =  1,
  pages    =  39,
  abstract = "BACKGROUND: Genomic alterations in 8 genes are now the targets of
              FDA-approved therapeutics in non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC),
              but their distribution according to genetic ancestry, sex,
              histology, and smoking is not well established. METHODS: Using
              multi-institutional genetic testing data from GENIE, we
              characterize the distribution of targetable genomic alterations in
              8 genes among 8675 patients with NSCLC (discovery cohort: DFCI, N
              = 3115; validation cohort: Duke, Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer
