               FinnGen (500,348 individuals), All of US (169,312 individuals),
               and Million Veteran Program (451,206 individuals). We also
               estimated associations in cancer-specific consortia. RESULTS: No
               association was observed between genetically-predicted alcohol
               consumption and overall cancer (odds ratio (OR) per 1 standard
