  journal  = "Genome Res.",
  volume   =  31,
  number   =  10,
  pages    = "1913--1926",
  abstract = "The tumor immune microenvironment is a main contributor to cancer
              progression and a promising therapeutic target for oncology.
              However, immune microenvironments vary profoundly between
              patients, and biomarkers for prognosis and treatment response lack
              precision. A comprehensive compendium of tumor immune cells is
              required to pinpoint predictive cellular states and their spatial
              localization. We generated a single-cell tumor immune atlas,
              jointly analyzing published data sets of >500,000 cells from 217
              patients and 13 cancer types, providing the basis for a patient
