               decade has seen the emergence of new approaches based on
               coevolution, deep mutational scanning and genome-scale genetic or
               chemical–genetic interaction mapping that enable modelling of the
               structures of individual proteins or protein complexes. Here, we
               review the emerging use of large-scale genetic datasets and deep
               learning approaches to model protein structures and their
               interactions, and discuss the integration of structural data from
               different sources. Large-scale genetic datasets and deep learning
               approaches are being used to model the structures of proteins or
               protein complexes. This Review describes approaches based on
               coevolution, deep mutational scanning and genome-scale genetic or
               chemical–genetic interaction mapping and their application and
               integration to inform structural modelling.",
